          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:17:19Z",
          "note": "The PUT route previously had a host validation guard (rejecting paths with slashes/whitespace and prototype-pollution keys). The new GitCredentialEntry model does not impose such restrictions on host — the host field is a plain string identifier and validation is left to the caller. If stricter host validation is desired in future (e.g. rejecting hosts with path separators), it can be added as a separate concern. Current behaviour is correct per spec."
        },
        {
          "type": "refactor",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:17:19Z",
          "note": "buildMaskedCredentials() and generateUniqueId() are module-private helpers in config.ts. If more credential utility functions accumulate, consider extracting them to a dedicated src/server/routes/credential-utils.ts to keep config.ts focused on route registration."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:17:19Z",
          "note": "The generateUniqueId() function falls back to 'credential' when toKebabCase(label) returns an empty string (all-special characters). A more descriptive fallback (e.g. 'unnamed-credential') could improve usability in edge cases."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T10:18:17Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T10:20:55Z",
      "duration_ms": 158000,
      "summary": [
        "Full Verification Stack executed for WP-005 credential endpoint routes.",
        "Build check: TypeScript compilation produces 4 known errors in orchestrator files (repository-orchestrator.ts, workspace-orchestrator.ts and their tests) — all confirmed out-of-scope for WP-005 per Developer handoff notes.",
        "AC verification: All 8 acceptance criteria verified via test execution and manual code review.",
        "Regression testing: All 331 server integration tests pass (74 credential-specific + 257 other server tests), zero failures.",
        "Edge-case stress tests: Verified all-special-character label fallback to 'credential', collision chain resolution beyond -9 suffix, empty/short token masking, and whitespace trimming behaviour.",
        "No implementation defects found. The duplicate-ID scenario (AC6) is handled through upsert semantics (explicit id match → update in-place) and suffix generation (auto-id path); no 400 rejection path is triggered because the logic structurally prevents duplicates."
