        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
          "note": "MEDIUM — A02 (Cryptographic Failures) / A09 (Security Logging): Git tokens (Personal Access Tokens) are stored as plaintext in config.json on disk. This is an inherent design constraint (the tool must use the raw token to authenticate git operations), but it creates risk if the config file is world-readable or included in backups/version control. Recommendation: Ensure config.json is created with restrictive file permissions (0600) at install time, and add it to .gitignore. Consider adding a note in documentation. No code change required for WP-005."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
          "note": "MEDIUM — A09 (Security Logging & Monitoring Failures): PUT and DELETE /api/config/credentials endpoints mutate security-sensitive credentials (add, update, delete tokens) with no audit log. If unauthorized access to the config API occurs, there is no trail to detect it. Recommendation: Add structured log entries (e.g. 'Credential created: id=X', 'Credential deleted: id=X') on successful mutations, without logging token values. This is a systemic gap across the config routes, not specific to WP-005."
        },
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
          "note": "MEDIUM — A04 (Insecure Design): The host field in PUT /api/config/credentials accepts any non-empty string with no format or scheme validation. A previous guard (rejecting slashes, whitespace, prototype-pollution keys) was removed in WP-005 to accommodate the new GitCredentialEntry model. While the host field is not used in file-system operations or shell commands in this WP's scope, if downstream code uses host to construct git remote URLs or shell arguments without further sanitization, this could become a higher-severity injection vector. File: src/server/routes/config.ts, PUT /api/config/credentials handler (~line 200). Recommendation: Add lightweight host format validation (e.g. reject values containing path separators or URL scheme prefixes) as a defence-in-depth measure. Track for resolution before host values are used in any system calls."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
