          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
          "note": "LOW — A03 (Injection / Information Exposure): The DELETE route echoes back the caller-supplied credId value in a 404 error message: 'No credential entry found with id \"${credId}\".'. This is not exploitable in a local-only deployment context, but reflects user-controlled input in error responses. Recommendation: Consider a generic message ('Credential not found.') or sanitize the echoed ID to a known-safe character set before inclusion in error text."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
