      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:20:55Z",
      "notes": [
        "WP-005 QA PASS. All 8 acceptance criteria verified. 331/331 server tests pass. Credential routes (GET/PUT/DELETE /api/config/credentials) operate correctly with GitCredentialEntry[] format, masked tokens, kebab-case ID generation, upsert semantics, and suffix disambiguation. The 4 TypeScript errors in orchestrator files are out-of-scope for this WP. Ready for Security Audit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:22:52Z",
      "notes": [
        "WP-005 security audit PASS. 0 Critical, 0 High findings. Token masking is correct and consistent; input validation is solid; body size limit enforced at 1 MB. Three Medium observations noted (plaintext token storage in config.json, missing audit logging on credential mutations, unvalidated host field format) and two Low observations (no per-field length limits, user-controlled text in a 404 error message) — none are blocking. Code is ready for Code Review. Reviewer should pay particular attention to the host field validation gap (Medium) as a potential downstream injection risk if host values are ever used in system calls."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

